        def freeze(self, ) -> ApexGraphHandle:
        
            Holds a copy of an input value.
            
            Value nodes have multiple purposes:
            
              * You can introduce a new value to the graph by creating a Value node
                of a specific type, and then setting its value in the node parameter
                window (select the Value node and press [P] to display the node
                parameter window).
            
              * When the parm input port is connected, the Value node creates a copy
                of the incoming data. This copy can be used to prevent race
                conditions when multiple nodes attempt to modify the same value in
                place, that is, without making a copy of the value (in-place ports
                are indicated by square port shapes). Value nodes can be used to
                create multiple copies of a value, which when piped into an in-place
                port, allows the node with the in-place port to have its own copy of
                the value to modify.
            
